course: dictionary
lesson: 10094
title: They: a small word with big jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «They» is a small word that stands in for names. Instead of saying the same names again and again, you can use «they» for the people or things already named, when there is more than one. «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them, and they are just as much part of it.» Here «they» means the children, so you can swap in the children and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «They» can also mean people in general, as in «They say it will rain». It can even stand for one person when you do not know, or do not say, if the person is a boy or a girl. Look at the words around it to work out who «they» means.
explain: Check your answer by swapping the noun into the sentence in place of «they». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right person or thing.
fact: «They» is a pronoun, a word that takes the place of a noun.
fact: Related pronouns are «them», «their», «theirs» and «themselves».
fact: «They» means the people or things already named, more than one.
fact: «They» can mean people in general, as in «They say it will rain».
fact: In formal writing, such as exams, writers avoid «they» and repeat the noun instead, for example «the pupils» in place of «they».
exercise: «When they bow, their curly wigs get tangled, and Alice has to run off to hide her laughter.» Who does «they» mean? | *The people who bow | Alice | The wigs | The laughter
exercise: «Older children in big families often help a lot, but they still need breakfast, sleep and time for themselves.» Who does «they» mean? | Breakfast | Teachers | Parents | *Older children in big families
exercise: Mia says, «They say it will rain.» Who is «they» here? | Mia's brother only | *People in general | A boy named Sam | The weather forecasters' rain
test: «They're closing the pool», says Ali. In this casual talk, who does «they» mean? | The pool | Two children | The swimmers only | *The people in charge
test: In «Ali and Sam lost their bags, so they went back», who does «they» mean? | The bags | Mum | *Ali and Sam | The bus driver
exam: In formal writing, which words best replace «they» in «Some children are adopted: they join a family»? | A parent | Adoption | Families | *The children
